Failover
--------

The simulation in the Failover game is a TypeScript port of Server Survival by
Kostyantyn Pshenychnyy, released under the MIT license.

  Source:   https://github.com/pshenok/server-survival
  Revision: 7804e5969e28267cd33837e023eb46fa65da72b7
  License:  MIT, full text in src/components/game/failover/LICENSE-server-survival.txt

Changes: ported to TypeScript; audio, art and strings replaced or rewritten.
Behavior changes: the simulation runs on a fixed 20 Hz step with seeded random
streams instead of the frame rate and Math.random; and demolishing a dead-letter
queue re-homes the requests parked in it, where upstream leaves them stranded.


Script Knight
-------------

The engine and the tower data in the Script Knight game
(src/components/game/script-knight/engine/) are ported from WarriorJS,
https://github.com/olistic/warriorjs, at commit bc68e87.

  Copyright (c) 2015-present Matias Olivera. MIT License. The licence text is
  in src/components/game/script-knight/engine/LICENSE.

The port is modified by Amin Dhouib, 2026: it is rewritten in TypeScript, adds
a step API, an instance logger, unit ids and direction checks, and hands the
player's code a frozen per-turn facade.

WarriorJS is itself a port of ruby-warrior by Ryan Bates,
https://github.com/ryanb/ruby-warrior (MIT License). It is credited as the
original idea; no ruby-warrior code is used here. The WarriorJS logo is not
used.
